summary:
- topic: SPHS Marching Band Recognition
  text: The meeting began with a celebration of the South Portland High School Marching
    Band, who won a gold medal at the state finals. Band Director Jen Fletcher spoke
    about the team's hard work and successful season, and the board presented certificates
    to all student members and staff.
- topic: Financial Update and Outlook
  text: Finance Director Abigail Ketchen presented a financial update, noting that
    a one-time geothermal energy tax credit of over $800,000 will help the district
    avoid a deficit this fiscal year. However, she warned of significant future challenges
    due to rising costs and the depletion of the district's fund balance, which has
    historically been used to buffer tax increases.
- topic: South Portland Middle School Field Issues
  text: Director of Operations Mike Nalli reported on the ongoing issues with the
    SPMS athletic field, detailing problems with soil quality, compaction, and weeds.
    He outlined a multi-step remediation plan, and the board discussed holding the
    original contractor financially responsible for the failures.
- topic: Teachers' Contract Ratified
  text: The board unanimously voted to ratify the new three-year contract with the
    South Portland Teachers’ Association (SPTA). Board members and union representatives
    expressed relief and gratitude for reaching an agreement after a lengthy negotiation
    process.
- topic: Public Urges Support Staff Contract Settlement
  text: During public comment, multiple teachers and union leaders, including the
    presidents of the SPTA and SPESPA, urged the board to quickly settle the contract
    for the educational support professionals (SPESPA). Speakers highlighted the crucial
    role of ed techs, clerks, and office managers and called for the board to extend
    the same urgency to these negotiations.
- topic: Education Foundation Progress
  text: SPMS Principal Rebecca Stern provided an update on the formation of a new
    South Portland Schools Education Foundation. The committee is developing a mission,
    creating a board, and has partnered with the University of Maine Law School's
    business clinic to establish its 501(c)(3) nonprofit status.
- topic: Farewell to Outgoing Board Members
  text: As it was the last regular meeting before the election, the board shared farewells
    for outgoing members, including Chair Tandy Ratliff and Member Susan Rauscher.
    Fellow board members thanked them for their service, leadership, and calm demeanor
    during a challenging period for the district.
